# Rockman 6 (J) main text font, "A=$0B" table. Byte = BG tile number (CHR set $81 / $D2 source: PRG bank $10 +$1000, file 0x21010, 121 tiles).
# Used by: intro, ending (CAPCOM TIMES), password/GAME OVER/CONTINUE messages, YOU GET screens, boss-intro data values, staff-roll names, PUSH START-less screens.
# Codes $00-$25 are shared by the bold Latin fonts of the boss-intro and YOU GET screens (different glyph art, same codes).
# Dakuten/handakuten are SEPARATE tiles written after the kana: ば = $59 $3E (は゛), ぱ = $59 $27 (は゜).
# $2F is a second blank (used as the space inside picture frames and the staff roll). $32 is the "r." ligature of Dr./Mr. ($0E $32 = Dr., $17 $32 = Mr.).
# Only 16 katakana exist: イクシストフホマラリ ルロワンッュ (+ ー). No kanji anywhere in the text.
# Measured live from CHR-RAM in the intro (frame 1800), ending, password screen and staff roll [seen].
